# Feature landing pages (site architecture — always)

Patron feature landings (VIP reserV, floqCast, ShoutOut, and future products) share **one** header + venue-search pattern. Same Site chrome, same hierarchy, **different feature icon only**. Do **not** put the FloqR parent logo on feature landings — FloqR branding stays on Search / Welcome hubs.

Resume: `@feature-landing$` / `$feature-landing$`.

Shared module: `floqr-feature-landing.js` + `floqr-feature-landing.css` (`window.FLOQRFeatureLanding`).

## Canonical header stack (top → bottom)

1. **Back** — `floqrGlobalBack` / `FLOQRNav.applyGlobalBack` (← Back to Search). No hardcoded `?v=` in the href.
2. **Feature icon only** — chrome pack via `data-floqr-chrome-icon` (VIP / ShoutOut / floqCast). Centered in `.product-brand-stack`. **No** `.product-parent-logo` / FloqR mark on the landing.
3. **Feature title + `?`** — one flex row (`.{feature}-title-row` / `.feature-landing-title-row` / `.floqr-page-title-row`): `<h1 class="floqr-page-title">` + `details.help-popout` summary `?`. **Font size = Appearance panel h2** (`--floqr-page-title-size` → `--floqr-title-size`). Same schema as Profile & Settings. Intro / how-to copy lives **inside** the `?`, not as a long paragraph under the title.
4. **Body card** — glass card. Section head **Choose a venue** + `?` (`.feature-landing-section-head`). Search input + status line + result grid.

### Forbidden header layouts

- FloqR parent logo above or beside the feature icon on a feature landing.
- Feature icon **on the same line** as a FloqR logo.
- Legacy `suprstr-logo.png` as the floqCast mark — use chrome pack / `floqcast-hero-icon.svg` only as fallback.
- Flat admin `#111` body on product landings — see `design-notes-product-chrome.mdc`.

## Venue / contextual search (required)

- GPS → IP → profile via `FLOQRGeoSearch` / `FLOQRFeatureLanding.resolvePatronLocation`.
- Empty search: **top 4 nearest** venues that allow the feature (`NEARBY_TOP = 4`).
- Typing: all matches, still nearest-first. Haystack includes name, brand, city, genres, event names.
- Cards use `FLOQRFeatureLanding.renderVenueCardHtml` with **feature-specific facts**:
  - **ShoutOut** — LED sizes supported, patron custom ShoutOuts yes/no, template count, nights
  - **VIP reserV** — open days, min deposit, dress code, age, genres
  - **floqCast** — screen size, sound yes/no/ask, floqCast board size, genres
  - **General Search** — contact, category/genre, FLOQR public page, website, social handles
- CTA: **Select venue** (feature may then continue: Go live / floor map / Throw ShoutOut).

## Color / chrome

Same Site chrome tokens as Search (`FLOQRChromeScheme` / `isSiteChrome`). Load `floqr-chrome-scheme.js` on every feature landing that uses `data-floqr-chrome-icon`. Primary CTA = hot→accent gradient.

**Required:** early-paint `data-floqr-chrome` from `localStorage floqr.isSiteChrome` (same head snippet as `index.html` / `patron-portal.html`) **before** CSS. Body wash for `body.floqcast-page` / `body.shoutout-search-page` / `body.vip-page` lives in `floqr-feature-landing.css` per scheme — **never** pin Nightlife with `!important` in feature CSS.

## Icons — one mark, two surfaces

| Surface | Asset |
|---|---|
| Search tile face | Chrome pack JPG/PNG via `data-floqr-chrome-icon` |
| Feature landing hero | **Same** chrome pack (no FloqR parent) |
| Display / idle (floqCast board) | `images/chrome/floqcast-nightlife.jpg` |

## Checklist (new or edited feature landing)

- [ ] Header: Back → feature icon (no FloqR) → title + `?`
- [ ] Early-paint `data-floqr-chrome` + loads `floqr-feature-landing.js` + `.css` + `floqr-geo-search.js` + chrome scheme
- [ ] Body wash follows selected Site chrome (not Nightlife-locked)
- [ ] Empty list = nearest 4; status line shows place/source
- [ ] Cards show feature-specific facts + Select venue
- [ ] `?` mirrored in `floqai-help-repository.js` + i18n help packs
- [ ] No hardcoded `?v=` in nav links
- [ ] Update `docs/FEATURE-WIRING.md`

